---
import Article from '../layouts/Article.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, GITHUB_URL } from '../data/site';

const path = '/privacy';
const title = 'Privacy Policy - sshkeygen.dev';
const description =
  'sshkeygen.dev collects nothing: no cookies, no analytics, no tracking and no network requests for your keys. Keys are generated and kept only in your browser.';
---

<Article
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  crumb="Privacy"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  lead="We collect nothing. Keys are generated in your browser and never leave it."
  articleType="WebPage"
  updated="2026-10-08"
  cta={false}
>
  <p>Last updated 8 October 2026.</p>

  <h2 id="keys">Keys and passphrases</h2>
  <p>
    Keys, passphrases and any key you paste into the fingerprint checker exist only in your browser tab's memory. They
    are never transmitted, stored or logged, and they are gone when you close or reload the tab or press clear.
    Downloads are saved by your browser without involving our server.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every page carries a Content Security Policy with <code>connect-src 'none'</code>, so the page cannot open network
    connections from script. The source is on <a href={GITHUB_URL} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="analytics">Cookies, analytics and tracking</h2>
  <p>
    None. No cookies, no analytics, no ads, no third-party content. Fonts are self-hosted. Links to Termphin carry only
    campaign tags naming this site and the place on the page.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hosting">Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    The web server receives what every browser sends, such as your IP address, the page requested and your user agent.
    This may be kept briefly in standard logs for security and operations. It is not used to identify you and never
    contains keys.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    Changes are published on this page with a new date. Privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</Article>
